{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.PosDef","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero"],"declarations":33,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.inactive_dual_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.inactive_dual_zero","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L253-L253","doc":"Off the active set, the dual variable is exactly zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.active_dual_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.active_dual_pos","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L251-L251","doc":"On the active set, the dual variable is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.active","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.active","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L249-L249","doc":"The active set: indices where the dual variable is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.mk","kind":"ctor","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L246-L246","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.toStrongDualityPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.toStrongDualityPair","kind":"def","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L246-L253","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair","kind":"structure","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L228-L253","doc":"**Strict-complementarity certificate.**\n\nStrengthens `StrongDualityPair` with the active/inactive\npartition of the constraint indices.  An index `i` is \"active\"\niff its dual variable `ystar i` is strictly positive (constraint\nis binding); otherwise it is \"inactive\" with `ystar i = 0`.\n\nConcrete fields:\n* `active : Set ι` — the active set\n* `active_dual_pos` — `∀ i ∈ active, 0 < ystar i`\n* `inactive_dual_zero` — `∀ i ∉ active, ystar i = 0`\n\nThe \"strict\" qualifier means the dichotomy is sharp: there is\nno ambiguous case where both `ystar i > 0` and the slack is\npositive.  This is the Todd 2001 §3.4 / Boyd-Vandenberghe §5.5\nformulation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualSlack_trace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualSlack_trace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L194-L217","doc":"**Key algebraic identity**: `tr(S(y) · Φ) = objAt Φ -\ndualObjAt y` for any feasible `Φ`.  Combines\n`Matrix.trace_add` / `_smul` / `_sub` with feasibility\n(`tr(A_i · Φ) = b_i`).\n\nPROOF: linearity of trace + feasibility constraints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualObjAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualObjAt","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L190-L192","doc":"**Dual objective value** at a dual point `y`: `Σ_i y_i · b_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualSlack","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualSlack","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L185-L188","doc":"**Dual slack matrix** `S(y) := T - Σ_i y_i · A_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.strong_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.strong_duality","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L165-L172","doc":"**Strong duality** (per-instance form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality.pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality.pair","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L163-L163","doc":"A strong-duality pair exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality.mk","kind":"ctor","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L160-L160","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality","kind":"class","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L152-L163","doc":"**Strong-duality typeclass**: witnesses that an SDP satisfies\nthe primal-dual identity (Slater's condition + strong duality\nfor convex problems, Boyd-Vandenberghe §5.2.3 + §5.3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.obj_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.obj_eq","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L150-L150","doc":"Strong-duality identity — `opaque marker` for genuinely-open\ninfrastructure: the content-bearing ℝ-specialised field is\n`RealStrongDualityPair.obj_eq_dualObj`\n(`objAt Φstar = dualObjAt ystar`, in\n`QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRealUniqueness`). Kept `True` here so the\ngeneric skeleton stays usable by the empty-constraint witness\n`trivialStrongDualityPair`; consume the ℝ form for the real\nobjective-equality content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.dual_feas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.dual_feas","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L141-L141","doc":"Dual feasibility — `opaque marker` for genuinely-open\ninfrastructure: PSD-ness `(sdp.dualSlack ystar).PosSemidef`\nrequires `[Fintype ι]` + the `StarOrderedRing` of `R := ℝ`\nand so cannot be stated over the generic `R` carrier here.\nThe content-bearing ℝ-specialised field is\n`RealStrongDualityPair.dualSlack_psd` (in\n`QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRealUniqueness`); consume that, not this\nabstract skeleton. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.primal_feas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.primal_feas","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L132-L132","doc":"Primal feasibility witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.ystar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.ystar","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L130-L130","doc":"Dual-optimal point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.Φstar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.Φstar","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L128-L128","doc":"Primal-optimal point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.mk","kind":"ctor","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L126-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair","kind":"structure","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L115-L150","doc":"**Strong duality witness** — abstract skeleton for any\n`R : Type*` (with appropriate algebraic structure).  Per\nCopilot review: the `dual_feas` and `obj_eq` fields are\nintentionally `True` placeholders here because PSD-ness\ncannot be expressed without `[Fintype ι]` and `R := ℝ`.\n\nThe **ℝ-specialised** form `RealStrongDualityPair` (in\n`QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRealUniqueness`) carries the actual\nPSD-ness + objective-equality content.  Downstream code\nthat needs the categorical content should consume that\nstructure, not this abstract skeleton. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual.y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual.y","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The dual variables, one per primal equality constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual.mk","kind":"ctor","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual","kind":"structure","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L98-L102","doc":"**Dual SDP** derived from the primal: maximise `Σ b_i y_i` over\n`y : ι → R` subject to `T - Σ y_i A_i ⪰ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.objAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.objAt","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L94-L96","doc":"**Primal-feasible objective value** at a given feasible point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.isFeasible_of_emptyConstraints","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.isFeasible_of_emptyConstraints","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**Empty-constraint feasibility** — proved theorem. With no\nequality constraints, every PSD matrix is feasible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.feasible_of_strictlyFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.feasible_of_strictlyFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L75-L82","doc":"**Strictly feasible implies feasible** — proved theorem.\nA positive-definite matrix is positive-semidefinite, so any\nSlater-witness is automatically a feasible point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.IsStrictlyFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.IsStrictlyFeasible","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L68-L73","doc":"**Slater-strict feasibility**: there exists a positive-definite\n`Φ ≻ 0` (not just PSD) satisfying every equality constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.IsFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.IsFeasible","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L64-L66","doc":"**Feasibility predicate** for an SDP candidate `Φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.rhs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.rhs","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Right-hand sides of equality constraints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.constraint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.constraint","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Equality-constraint operators (one per index `i : ι`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.cost","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The cost operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal","kind":"structure","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L49-L60","doc":"**Primal SDP problem data.**\n\nA semidefinite program: minimise `⟨T, Φ⟩ := tr(T · Φ)` over\n`Φ ⪰ 0` subject to equality constraints `tr(A_i · Φ) = b_i`\nfor each `i : ι`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}